## Context
STATE.md backlog records: "CI required-checks rule disabled 2026-05-26 —
**re-enable** (talk done, no longer blocking)." The Econom'IA talk was
delivered 2026-05-27, so the temporary relaxation of branch protection is no
longer needed. The rule was disabled to unblock pre-talk slide merges; merges
since (#619–#624) went through without required checks gating them.

## Actions
1. Decide which checks to require on `main` (the test/lint workflow(s) that
   were gating before 2026-05-26).
2. Re-enable required status checks in the `main` branch-protection rule
   (forge settings / `gh api`), matching the pre-2026-05-26 configuration.
3. Confirm a trivial PR is now gated by the required check(s) before closing.
4. Remove the backlog note from STATE.md.

## Verification
- [ ] Branch-protection on `main` lists the required check(s) again.
- [ ] A test PR cannot merge until the required check passes.
- [ ] STATE.md backlog line removed.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Required status checks re-enabled on `main`; STATE.md backlog note cleared.
